= BITwiki Charter =

The Charter describes how BITwiki conducts knowledge work. It is an operating covenant, not a replacement for the [[BITwiki:Manifesto|Manifesto]] or [[BITwiki:Constitution|Constitution]].

== Purpose ==

BITwiki exists to develop and preserve structured knowledge through research, discussion, computation, experimentation, review, and revision.

The wider ecosystem supports multidisciplinary research, development, and knowledge exchange. Its work is multi-scale, modular, openly extensible, and intended to bridge disciplines rather than isolate them.

== Commitments ==

=== Preserve signal ===
Recover source material before interpretation. Do not silently replace an authored claim with a summary of what an editor thinks it means.

=== Verify before canon ===
A discussion should move into BITwiki only after the relevant research has been conducted properly, reviewed, and accepted as worth preserving. Important claims should be source-backed. AI output is assistance, not authority.

=== Keep perspective explicit ===
BITwiki does not claim perfect neutrality. Distinguish evidence, interpretation, hypothesis, worldview, metaphor, and speculation when the distinction changes how a reader should understand a claim.

=== Revise recursively ===
First revisions are not sacred. Useful outputs should be reviewed, corrected, compared, improved, and reused.

=== Prefer slow, surgical improvement ===
Slow, surgical, intelligent small wins are preferred over rash changes involving too many components at once. Compound improvements while preserving recoverability.

=== Preserve provenance ===
Moves, merges, transclusions, rewrites, and schema changes must not erase where knowledge came from or how it evolved.

=== Preserve complexity that carries meaning ===
Remove accidental complexity, duplication, broken scaffolding, and obsolete implementation assumptions. Do not remove a distinction merely because it is difficult, unusual, philosophical, or inconvenient.

=== Keep public and protected knowledge separate ===
Public Git and public BITwiki contain public material. Private memory, credentials, access-control internals, unpublished sensitive material, and identity-bound state require separate boundaries.

== Human–AI collaboration ==

Humans, agents, Constructs, and workflows may participate in knowledge production. Their output should remain reviewable and correctable.

The goal of automation is not maximal automation. It is to make research, reasoning, context, verification, and reuse more capable while preserving human dignity and agency.

== Contribution standard ==

High-signal participation makes the system clearer, more accurate, more useful, or more reusable. Volume is not signal.

== Stewardship ==

Stewardship means maintaining fidelity in the knowledge continuum: helping useful work survive its original context without freezing the corpus against future correction.

The Charter should itself remain revisionable. Major revisions should preserve previous versions and explain the reason for change.

